  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Spices from the core source</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The company Pacific SpiZes focuses on processing and exporting spices from Moluccas, Indonesia, the core source of spices such as nutmeg, mace and cloves. The spices are eventually also imported by Pacific SpiZes (NL) and sold within the EU. By exporting nutmeg and mace in cooperation with a local collector, Kamboti Rempah Maluku, the company aims to increase the capacity of local nutmeg farmers. Pacific SpiZes pays a fair price to the local farmers and supports decent jobs. To be able to import the first container of spices DGGF-TA provided support to pre-finance one mixed (nutmeg and mace) container. With this project, 615 indirect jobs were supported amongst the local farmers and Kamboti Rempah Maluku. Capacity building in the form of training supported 395 people. Looking forward, Pacific SpiZes and Kamboti Rempah Maluku will join their forces by establishing a joint venture (Kamboti Pacific SpiZes PT) to further deepen the business relations and further focus on the training and education of farmers, to get the various certifications on Food Safety and the Rainforest Alliance sustainability certification.</narrative>
  </description>
